    "prototype_id": "A03",
    "title": "Spinach Κάτω Κάμπος: mildew conditions, but it is in harvest – do NOT spray",
    "body": "Same wet nights after the rain (leaf-wet 11-13 h per night). This lot is being cut now (safe since Mon 9 Nov). Any fungicide now would lock harvest for 7-14 days and break supply.",
    "action": "Keep cutting (~15 crates/day) Tue 17-Fri 20 Nov and Mon 23-Sat 28 Nov; not Thu before ~10:00 thaw, not in the rain Fri pm-Sun. Scout lower-leaf undersides each cut; grade out leaves with grey-violet growth.",
    "why_rule": "If a planting is harvesting AND a spray's PHI would block cuts before the end of its harvest window, the app does not recommend a spray; it recommends faster harvest + scouting.",
    "severity": "medium"
  },
  "notes": "J09 time 10:45 is parsed from the job notes. safe_since = 2 Nov 10:45 + 7 d."
